AGPL isolation (important)
  This engine is a clean, self-contained reimplementation of the "face-swap over
  a live camera → virtual camera" data flow. It uses only permissively-licensed
  libraries:
    - insightface  (MIT)         -> face detection/alignment + INSwapper swap
      (upstream states the Python library code is MIT; pinned to 1.0.1 because the
       0.7.x line ships no wheel and must be compiled on the user's machine)
    - onnxruntime  (MIT)
    - opencv-python (Apache-2.0) -> camera capture / frame handling
    - pyvirtualcam (MIT)         -> virtual camera output
    - fastapi / uvicorn (MIT)    -> localhost control API only
  The upstream project Deep-Live-Cam is AGPL-3.0. Its code is NOT linked, NOT
  vendored, and NOT copied here; it served only as behavioral reference. This
  directory contains zero AGPL-licensed source.

Process boundary
  This runs as a separate process in a separate venv created at runtime under
  <STATE_DIR>/faceswap/venv. The main backend (src/novelvideo) talks to it only
  over 127.0.0.1 HTTP and never imports it, so no copyleft obligation propagates
  into the Elastic-2.0 distribution.

Model weights
  Face-swap model weights (insightface inswapper_128, buffalo_l, GFPGAN, etc.)
  are downloaded by the user at runtime and are NOT bundled in this repository.
  Their licenses (largely non-commercial / research) are the user's own
  responsibility; the control panel and docs surface this notice.
